---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<section>
		<article class="mb-5">
			<h1>Tattoo Removal</h1>
			<p class="text-xl bg-[#EEE8E0] px-2">Post-Treatment Instructions</p>
		</article>
		<article>
			<div class="separation">
				<h2>What to Expect</h2>
				<p>	• Redness, swelling, whitening, pinpoint bleeding, or blistering may occur. <br>
					• The tattoo will gradually lighten over several treatments. <br>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="separation">
				<h2>Post-Treatment Care</h2>
				<p>	• Apply petrolatum or Bacitracin if instructed. <br>
					• Keep the area clean and covered for the first 24 hours. <br>
					• Change the dressing twice daily if directed. <br>
					• Do not pick blisters or scabs. <br>
					• Avoid swimming, hot tubs, and strenuous exercise for 48 hours. <br>
					• Wear Mineral SPF 50+ and avoid sun exposure until healed. <br>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="separation">
				<h2>Possible Side Effects</h2>
				<p>	• Common: redness, swelling, blistering, crusting. <br>
					• Less common: prolonged redness, temporary pigment changes. <br>
					• Rare: infection, scarring, allergic reactions. <br>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="separation">
				<h2>Contact kiwiMEDSPA Immediately</h2>
				<p>	• Increasing pain, pus, fever, excessive swelling, severe blistering, or any concerning symptoms. <br>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="separation">
				<h2>Treatment Schedule</h2>
				<p>	• Most tattoos require multiple sessions (4-10, could be more), spaced 6–8 weeks apart depending on tattoo characteristics. <br>
				</p>
			</div>

			<div class="separation">
				<h2>Questions?</h2>
				<p>kiwiMEDSPA Medical Weight Loss &amp; Aesthetics Dr. Sergio Angel, MD Dr. Allie Angel, MD</p>
				<p>470-310-8155</p>
			</div>
		</article>
	</section>
</Layout>
